   104	
   105	The right-hand side of the valley had gone silent. Not the whole valley — the wash side still ticked and whirred, the bird was still there somewhere behind them — but from the road to the valley wall on the right, for as far ahead as he could judge, the scrub had stopped making any sound at all. It was the shape of the silence Lira had heard. A hole in the noise, and the hole was keeping pace with them.
   106	
