   133	Brom's hand had not moved on the mule's cheek-strap. Cael had watched Brom answer anything with teeth for three years, and the answer had always been the same: to become the thing teeth broke on. He was not becoming it. He was walking at a mule's shoulder in the near dark with his shoulders down and his breathing slow, exactly as large as his body made him and not one degree larger, and once, when the buckle jingled, he said "Easy" to the mule in a voice that carried nowhere at all.
