   225	They stayed six days. The steading fed them for lofting the grain, which was not a contract and went on no board, and for a fence-post Brom reset because he could not walk past a leaning post. Lira ran the fence-line at first light each morning, because there was nothing at Thornwater to run at and she needed to run at something. Seln was gone for hours at a time and came back with the lay of every road out of the place, unasked, and once said "The wash goes round the north side" to Cael at supper as though it were the weather. Karis sat in the loft with the three boxes open around her and wrote, for most of one day, the single word the carter had given her at the gate, with a line under it, and beneath the line everything she had counted on the stretch, and beneath that nothing, because there was nothing beneath it yet.
