     5	Cael noticed that before he noticed her. She was a broad grey-braided woman of fifty or sixty with her sleeves rolled to the elbow, and she stood in the gap of her gate and counted them through it as a farmer counts sheep at a hurdle: the dark coat first, then the two of them abreast, and the mule, and the cart, and last a very large young man with a hedging bill. She moved her lips for each. When the tailboard was inside she put her shoulder to the gate and shut it, and dropped a bar as thick as his arm.
     6	
