     9	There was a platform beside the gate, on the inner face of the fence, six feet up, with a ladder to it. A man stood there. He had a bow in his left hand and an arrow on the string, and Cael had seen enough people threaten him to know that this one was not doing it. The bow hung at the length of his arm. The arrow pointed at the planks between his boots. He was looking out over the top of the posts, down the valley, at something a hundred and ten yards off beside a white stone, and he did not once look round at the people who had just come in under him.
