   109	She had made a table of it in her exact hand. At the head stood the word, underlined once, and under the word his five counts in the order he had given them: *keeps station at forty-five yards; makes no sound; follows the buckle with its head; will not cross the gravel fan; answers nothing, having been given nothing.* Beneath those stood the figure, *110*, and after it, in smaller writing, *of C.'s strides, gate to stone.* She had gone out to the well in the heat of noon and paced a hundred and ten of her own along the inside of the fence, which came to a good deal less, so as to know in her legs how far it was.
